# Git author for this repo

This is a personal/open-source project, NOT an Uber project. All commits and
pushes from this repo must be authored as **`Marcos Suarez <suarez84@gmail.com>`**,
never with the Uber email.

Never run `git config` to change the global identity. Override per-command instead:

```bash
git -c user.name="Marcos Suarez" -c user.email="suarez84@gmail.com" \
    commit -m "..." \
    --author="Marcos Suarez <suarez84@gmail.com>"
```

Or set env vars for a single command:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Marcos Suarez" GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="suarez84@gmail.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Marcos Suarez" GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="suarez84@gmail.com" \
  git commit -m "..."
```

## Pre-commit hook & GPG signing

The machine has Uber's tooling installed globally (an `asd-cli` pre-commit
hook AND `commit.gpgsign=true` with `gpg.format=x509` pointing at an Uber
x509 key that requires `ussh`). Both fail on this personal repo with
`no ssh cert is found, please run ussh first`.

The user has explicitly authorized bypassing both for commits in this repo.
Always pass **`--no-verify --no-gpg-sign`** when committing here:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Marcos Suarez" GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="suarez84@gmail.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Marcos Suarez" GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="suarez84@gmail.com" \
  git commit --no-verify --no-gpg-sign -m "..."
```

## Pushing to prod

`origin/main` on https://github.com/kyberis/etracker is wired to Vercel; pushing
to `main` triggers a production deploy.

The pre-push hook is also Uber's `asd-cli` and fails the same way as the
pre-commit hook. Always push with **`--no-verify`**:

```bash
git push --no-verify origin main
```
